   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">31 May 2019 | News Release: https://www.adb.org/news/adb-backing-high-tech-systems-maldives-promote-trade</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Currently in MED BOLI system, functionalities have been developed and tested to exchange permit information directly with Customs. For other CBRA system, relevant APIs for integration will be made available by Customs in August 2022. Discussions were held with Customs in June and July 2022 to expedite availability of APIs for other CBRA system.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">E-transaction bill submitted to Parliament in August 2021, E-transaction Bill enacted on 27 April 2022.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Grant 0646: 72% of contracts awarded and 40% disbursed as of 02 May 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Loan 3794: 68% of contracts awarded and 37% disbursed as of 02 May 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">National Steering Committee on Data Harmonization formally established by President Office in August 2021. Except premises registry related standards, all key standards relevant for NSW project submitted to National Steering Committee on Data Harmonization for formal adoption and publication in early August 2021. Formal adoption and publication process is on-going.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Premises registry standards is carried out as part of the work initiated nationally to harmonize data in all Govt ICT systems, requires more consultation with stakeholders and will not impact delivery of NSW project.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Some results are in the Audited Project Financial Statements | Jun 2024: https://www.adb.org/sites/default/files/project-documents/51330/51330-001-apfs-en_3.pdf</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: NSW system is under rebidding process for system development and pilot test NSW phase 1. Bids received on 30 May 2022. Bid evaluation panel held introductory first meeting on 25 July 2022. Estimated time for completion of bid evaluation is mid-Aug 2022. Technical bid evaluation report was received on 27 October 2022. Financial bids were opened on 14 November 2022, evaluation is ongoing. NSW system is under rebidding process for system development and pilot test NSW phase 1. Technical bid evaluation report was received on 27 October 2022.NSW system is under rebidding process for system development and pilot test NSW phase 1. Technical bid evaluation report was received on 27 October 2022.NSW system is under rebidding process for development pilot test NSW phase 1NSW system is under rebidding process for development pilot test NSW phase 1NSW system is under rebidding process for development pilot test NSW phase 1E-transaction bill submitted to Parliament in August 2021, first reading completed and is currently at the committee stage. E-transaction Bill enacted on 27 April 2022.Dissemination of the findings of pilot testing is tentatively scheduled in Q1 2023.Pilot test for utilizing blockchain technology in trade facilitation has been ongoing since September 2020 and is estimated to be completed by Q4 2022.</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
   <indicator measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">TA 9739: 70% disbursed as of 02 May 2025</narrative>
    </title>
   </indicator>
